[[File:Multi Shot (Beta 58.0).png|thumb|Beta 58.0]]
When released in '''Beta 11.0 '''as a new version of the "Passive Buffer" spell [[Shootout]] was for a while, Multi Shot costed 6G. '''Beta 18.1''' dropped this to 5G. '''Beta 37.0''' reworked it completely.
Now, at a cost of 1G (making it the first time a Justice spell ever costed as low as this), it will deal 1 DMG to a monster of your choice. If the monster dies from it, you will receive a new Multi Shot in your hand, allowing it to be endless like [[Fast Sanction]], but even more like [[Lancer|Spade]]. '''Beta 38.0''' buffed it by earning you back the 1G paid for it if the killed monster had => 2 base HP. The spell can now also target players.

'''Beta 47.0''' redesigned it. Now, for 2G, it adds a random Justice spell with a cost of 3G or more, and it will be added to your hand with its cost reduced by 3G. (This results in a 1G profit and access to 1 more of any of Justice's other spells aside from [[Blitz Quiz]].) This was redesigned again in '''Beta 58.0''', returning to 1G to deal 1 DMG. It can once again only target a monster, but will now always add 2 new Multi Shots to your hand when used. However, it will only add those if it wasn't generated. As such, the given Multi Shots will not give even more new ones. '''Beta 58.1''' slightly changed it by only making Multi Shots generated by other Multi Shots specifically not give new ones.

